## std::hash — the `Hashable` mixin (CEO ruling TEC-13).
##
## Wave 2 (#06.8) — migrated from resolve/stdlib/mod.rs Rust
## registrations into self-hosted library/std/src/hash.rx.
##
## Ruxen's hashing surface is intentionally thin: one mixin, one
## method that returns a single Int. Custom hashers / DOS-resistant
## random seeds / Hasher builder / BuildHasher are explicit v2 work.
## v1 ships exactly enough for `Map[K, V]` and `Set[T]` to key on
## user types via implicit `include Hashable`.
##
## The deprecated `Hash` (trait) → `Hashable` alias is re-established
## by `Resolver::fixup_bootstrapped_stdlib_modules` after bootstrap
## merge, so `Hash` as a trait name keeps resolving (the `Hash[K,V]`
## collection type has its own type-position resolution path and is
## unaffected).

mixin Hashable
  def hash_code -> Int
end
